 { We can extend the definition of an unprotected piece to one that has the same number of attackers and defenders (e.g., 1 attacker and 1 defender, or 2 attackers and 2 defenders, and so on) . This is because such a piece is tactically vulnerable in the same way as a piece with 0 attackers and 0 defenders. For example in this position, the d5 Knight has 1 attacker and 1 defender. Similar to the previous position, it remains vulnerable to tactics if we are able to add an attacker with tempo. } 1. { -KEY- } Re5 { Despite the addition of an attacker and a defender to the d5 Knight, the tactic works in exactly the same way. } Ne6 2. Rexd5 Rxd5 3. Rxd5 
 *

