 { We will occasionally find positions where it is difficult to divide our attention between multiple unprotected pieces to find the best tactic. In such situations, I recommend that you prioritise the targets to identify the unprotected piece that will most likely fall. The first approach is to look for unprotected pieces exposed to multiple potential lines of attack. They will be prone to all sorts of forks and skewers. In this example, the c8 Knight is exposed on every open line possible. Couple that with Black’s weak King, and White has a total of 5 ways to win the piece! } 1. { -KEY- } Qe6+ { Fork } ( 1. Qg4 { Fork } ) 
 ( 1. Qc4 { Fork } ) 
 ( 1. Qe8 { Fork } ) 
 ( 1. Qa8 { Pin } ) 

 *

