 { As I have explained in the Introduction, every time you approach a position, it is important to take stock of the material first. This will give you a clearer idea of what initial moves to consider. For example, when you are down a great amount of material, you should be looking for a mating attack, a perpetual check, or to win even more material back. You may even consider how many pieces you can afford to sacrifice. To maintain this mental clarity as you go deeper into your calculations, it is essential to track the material count with each subsequent mental move you make. Otherwise, you would have difficulty identifying the best variation. To familiarise you with this thought process, I will present two puzzles that require you to track material continuously. } 1. -- 
