 { 1. Count the material and identify any material imbalance 2. Identify existing/potential threats a. Unprotected/hanging pieces b. X-Ray attacks c. Mating possibilities d. Trappable pieces e. Pinned, pinnable, forkable, and skewerable pieces 3. Calculate candidate moves and reject poor moves by repeating the Burger Technique from the opponent’s perspective. Be sure to calculate at least one and a half moves ahead before deciding to reject it. Step 1: White is up one pawn. Step 2: The unprotected pieces are Black's a8 Rook and g6 Knight, and White's g1 Rook, e4 Queen, and e2 Bishop, which is also pinned. Since the Queen, Bishop, and e3 pawn are on the same file, they are skewerable pieces. White also has a few pairs of forkable pieces, such as the g1 Rook and the d2 King, the h1 Rook and e4 Queen, as well as the e2 Bishop and the e4 Queen. Black, on the other hand, only needs to worry about his trappable f2 Queen. The f2 Queen and f8 Rook are not considered skewerable because the Rook is extremely well protected. Step 3: Based on these ideas, find a few candidate moves and pick the best. } 1... { -KEY- } Rae8 { This should be the first move to consider. We are taking advantage of the skewerable pieces on the e-file. 1. Rfe8 is also a possible candidate move but it does not seem to have a clear advantage over the text move. Given that we are also attacking e3, White's move is forced. } 2. Qd3 { If you are not sure how to proceed here, you should repeat the three-step thought process. The key changes in the first two steps are that e3 is unprotected, the e2 Bishop is now protected, and the d3 Queen and d2 King are pinnable pieces. Subsequently, look through all the checks, captures and threats } ( 2. Rf1 Rxe4 3. Rxf2 ) 
Ne5 { Now that we realise the Queen and King are pinnable, it becomes obvious that the d4 pawn is pinned. On top of that, the d2 King and g1 Rook are still forkable pieces. These two key points make Ne5 easier to spot. } 3. dxe5 Rd8 { We win the Queen while White's King remains exposed. } ( 3... Rd8 3. Rf1 { Trying to skewer the Queen and Rook doesn't work. } Rxd3 { We take the Queen with check first... } 5. Kxd3 Rd8 { then move our f8 Rook with check... } 6. Kc3 Qxe2 { then save our Queen. } ) 

